<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rao Jodha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1416">1416</a>–1489</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rao Jodha was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rathore">Rathore</a> ruler of Marwar who founded the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jodhpur">Jodhpur</a> in 1459. After recovering his family's capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mandore">Mandore</a> from Mewar, he built a new capital on a rocky hill nearby, with the great fort of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehrangarh">Mehrangarh</a>. His many sons founded other states, among them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rao-bika">Rao Bika</a>, who established Bikaner.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rao-jodha.jpg" alt="Rao Jodha" width="220" height="345" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rao_Jodha.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
